{{Basis}}

'''Sukatization''' or '''Sukatisation''' is the acculturation of non-Sukatic populations or groups into a [[Sukatic peoples|Sukatic culture or society]]. The term also refers to the historical adoption of the [[Sukat language]] and culture in [[Byrak]] and [[Northern Meran]] during the early middle ages. It may also refer to the transliteration of languages into the [[Sukatic script]]. 

==Subsets==
===Qymishification===
{{Main|Qymishification}}

[[Qymishification]] is the main subset of sukatization, applying the principle to [[Culture of Qym|Qymish culture]], where non-Qymish peoples adopt it over their own as a form of cultural assimilation. This is either forced or voluntary, and has been observed in [[Qym]] since the formation of the [[Principality of Qym|principality]] in {{abbr|1453|1207 (Earth Year Equivalent)}} and accelerated with the rise of [[Qymish nationalism]] in the {{abbr|23rd century|1828 to 1911 (Earth Years Equivalent)}}.

